WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:07.140
Local quantized model names often include labels such as Q2, Q3, Q4, Q5, Q6, or Q8.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.800
At a high level, the number indicates the approximate weight precision family:

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.000
lower levels use less memory and usually accept more approximation,

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.520
while higher levels retain more information and require more space.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.750
Suffixes identify specific methods, group sizes,

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:23.570
or mixed-precision choices and are meaningful only in the context of that format and

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:24.160
runtime.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:28.355
Q4 variants are often a practical starting point because they provide substantial memory

00:00:28.355 --> 00:00:31.600
savings while preserving useful quality for many models and tasks.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.280
That is a heuristic, not a guarantee.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.920
A particular architecture may respond differently,

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:38.200
two Q4 methods may not behave identically,

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:42.210
and a coding or reasoning task may reveal losses that casual conversation does not.

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:45.080
Q2 and Q3 can make otherwise inaccessible models fit,

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:48.040
but aggressive compression increases quality risk.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.000
Q5 and Q6 consume more memory and may preserve behavior more closely.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.860
Q8 often approaches the memory cost of higher precision while remaining useful when

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:58.595
quality is prioritized and hardware has room.

00:00:58.595 --> 00:01:02.785
Speed does not increase monotonically as bits decrease; kernel efficiency, offload,

00:01:02.785 --> 00:01:05.065
memory fit, and hardware support all matter.

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:07.280
Choose candidates around the hardware boundary.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:08.930
If Q5 fits with context headroom,

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:12.440
compare it with Q4 rather than assuming the smaller one wins.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:14.090
If only Q3 fits fully on the GPU,

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:18.010
compare its quality and speed with a smaller model at Q4 or Q5.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:22.520
Quantization level is one decision among model family, parameter count, context, runtime,

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:23.120
and workload.
